#: ../../../devguide.rst:7
msgid "Build, setup and test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:9
msgid ""
"psutil makes extensive use of C code, so a C compiler and the Python "
"development headers are required. First clone the repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:12
msgid ""
"git clone https://github.com/giampaolo/psutil.git\n"
"cd psutil"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:17
msgid ""
"On Linux, FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD and Solaris, install the system deps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:19
msgid ""
"make install-sysdeps       # compiler + python headers\n"
"make install-sysdeps-test  # CLI tools used by tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:24
msgid ""
"On macOS, AIX and Windows there's no such target, see :ref:"
"`install_from_source`. Then, everywhere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:27
msgid ""
"make install-pydeps-dev    # python development deps (linters, etc)\n"
"make build                 # compile the C extension in place\n"
"make test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:33
msgid ""
"``make`` (via the :src:`Makefile`) is used for building, testing and general "
"development tasks, including on Windows (see below):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:36
msgid ""
"make clean\n"
"make test\n"
"make test-parallel\n"
"make test-memleaks\n"
"make coverage\n"
"make lint-all\n"
"make fix-all\n"
"make uninstall\n"
"make help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:48
msgid "To run a specific test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:50
msgid "make test ARGS=tests/test_system.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:54
msgid ""
"``make build`` compiles the extension in place, so you can import psutil "
"straight from the repo. No need to install it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:57
msgid ""
"Don't use ``sudo``, except for the ``install-sysdeps-*`` targets, which "
"invoke it themselves when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:60
msgid ""
"To target a specific Python version, pass ``PYTHON`` to every step, so that "
"the extension is built by the same interpreter that runs the tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:63
msgid ""
"make install-pydeps-dev PYTHON=python3.13\n"
"make build PYTHON=python3.13\n"
"make test PYTHON=python3.13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:70
msgid "Windows"
msgstr "Windows"

#: ../../../devguide.rst:72
msgid "The recommended way to develop on Windows is to use ``make``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:73
msgid ""
"For the build tools, Git Bash and GNU Make setup see :ref:`install_windows`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:74
msgid "Once inside a Git Bash shell, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:76
msgid ""
"make install-pydeps-dev\n"
"make build\n"
"make test-parallel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:85
msgid "Debug mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:87
msgid ""
"If you need to debug unusual situations or report a bug, you can enable "
"debug mode via the :envvar:`PSUTIL_DEBUG` environment variable. In this "
"mode, psutil may print additional information to stderr. Usually these are "
"non-severe error conditions that are ignored instead of causing a crash. "
"Unit tests automatically run with debug mode enabled. To enable debug mode "
"in UNIX (or on Windows + Bash):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:94
msgid ""
"$ PSUTIL_DEBUG=1 python3 test_script.py\n"
"psutil-debug [psutil/_psutil_linux.c:150]> setmntent() failed (ignored)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:99
msgid "On Windows using cmd.exe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:101
msgid ""
"set PSUTIL_DEBUG=1 && python.exe test_script.py\n"
"psutil-debug [psutil/arch/windows/proc.c:56]> ReadProcessMemory -> "
"ERROR_NOACCESS (ignored)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:107
msgid "Coding style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:109
msgid ""
"All style and formatting checks are enforced locally on each ``git commit`` "
"and via a GitHub Actions pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:112
msgid ""
"Python: follows `PEP-8`_, formatted and linted with ``black`` and ``ruff``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:113
msgid "C: generally follows `PEP-7`_, formatted with ``clang-format``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:114
msgid ""
"Other files (``.rst``, ``.toml``, ``.md``, ``.yml``): validated by linters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:116
msgid "The pipeline re-runs all checks for consistency (``make lint-all``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:118
msgid ""
"Run ``make fix-all`` before committing; it usually fixes Python issues (via "
"``black`` and ``ruff``) and C issues (via ``clang-format``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:122
msgid "Code organization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:124
msgid ""
"Not every API reaches C: many are implemented in python alone (on Linux, by "
"parsing ``/proc``). For those that do, a call travels down through the "
"platform-specific layers. Linux is used here as an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:128
msgid ""
"import psutil\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"psutil/__init__.py          public API, Process class\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"psutil/_pslinux.py          python layer: parses /proc, calls into C\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"psutil/_psutil_linux.c      C extension entry point (arg parsing)\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"psutil/arch/linux/*.c       platform-specific C implementation\n"
"                            + arch/posix/*.c   shared by POSIX\n"
"                            + arch/all/*.c     shared by everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:146
msgid "Where things live:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:148
msgid ""
"psutil/__init__.py                   # Public API (\"import psutil\")\n"
"psutil/_common.py                    # Generic utilities\n"
"psutil/_ntuples.py                   # Named tuples returned by psutil APIs\n"
"psutil/_enums.py                     # Enum containers\n"
"psutil/_ps{platform}.py              # OS-specific python wrapper\n"
"psutil/_psutil_{platform}.c          # OS-specific C extension (entry "
"point)\n"
"psutil/arch/all/*.c                  # C code common to all OSes\n"
"psutil/arch/posix/*.c                # C code common to POSIX OSes\n"
"psutil/arch/bsd/*.c                  # C code common to the BSDs\n"
"psutil/arch/{platform}/*.c           # OS-specific C implementation\n"
"tests/test_process.py                # Main process API tests\n"
"tests/test_system.py                 # Main system API tests\n"
"tests/test_{platform}.py             # OS-specific tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:165
msgid "Adding a new API"
msgstr ""

